{"title":"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2(alcumus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2(alcumus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square flag has a red cross of uniform width with a blue square in the center on a white background as shown. (The cross is symmetric with respect to each of the diagonals of the square.) If the entire cross (both the red arms and the blue center) takes up 36% of the area of the flag, what percent of the area of the flag is blue?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/0/7d027dc282ca2a60e22b88189223a3514a774a85.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2.5 cm);  pair[] A, B, C; real t = 0.2;  A[1] = (0,0); A[2] = (1,0); A[3] = (1,1); A[4] = (0,1); B[1] = (t,0); B[2] = (1 - t,0); B[3] = (1,t); B[4] = (1,1 - t); B[5] = (1 - t,1); B[6] = (t,1); B[7] = (0,1 - t); B[8] = (0,t); C[1] = extension(B[1],B[4],B[7],B[2]); C[2] = extension(B[3],B[6],B[1],B[4]); C[3] = extension(B[5],B[8],B[3],B[6]); C[4] = extension(B[7],B[2],B[5],B[8]);  fill(C[1]--C[2]--C[3]--C[4]--cycle,blue); fill(A[1]--B[1]--C[1]--C[4]--B[8]--cycle,red); fill(A[2]--B[3]--C[2]--C[1]--B[2]--cycle,red); fill(A[3]--B[5]--C[3]--C[2]--B[4]--cycle,red); fill(A[4]--B[7]--C[4]--C[3]--B[6]--cycle,red);  draw(A[1]--A[2]--A[3]--A[4]--cycle); draw(B[1]--B[4]); draw(B[2]--B[7]); draw(B[3]--B[6]); draw(B[5]--B[8]); [/asy]\" width=\"122\" height=\"122\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/9/7197aab7f5b9d3d05f0e7bf3b1821fbfe7da28d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 0.5\\qquad\\text{(B)}\\ 1\\qquad\\text{(C)}\\ 2\\qquad\\text{(D)}\\ 3\\qquad\\text{(E)}\\ 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"344\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The diagram can be quartered as shown:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/7/4a7bcd7a4570fa60ff6e1cb35a3022bef95b5892.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(0,5)--(5,5)--(5,0)--(0,0)); draw((0,1)--(4,5)); draw((1,0)--(5,4)); draw((0,4)--(4,0)); draw((1,5)--(5,1)); draw((0,0)--(5,5),dotted); draw((0,5)--(5,0),dotted); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\nand reassembled into two smaller squares of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, each of which looks like this:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/8/3f820cdb6c67538a1a453e16902ae8ead1ab3c4f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(0,5)--(5,5)--(5,0)--(0,0)); draw((0,1)--(4,1)--(4,5)); draw((1,0)--(1,4)--(5,4)); label(&quot;blue&quot;,(0.5,0.5)); label(&quot;blue&quot;,(4.5,4.5)); label(&quot;red&quot;,(0.5,4.5)); label(&quot;red&quot;,(4.5,0.5)); label(&quot;white&quot;,(2.5,2.5)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\nThe border in this figure is the former cross, which still occupies 36% of the area. Therefore the inner square occupies 64% of the area, from which we deduce that it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18d070e5904c0d5fef09a82118dee5e63d025ed6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.8k \\times 0.8k$\" width=\"88\" height=\"12\" />, and that one blue square must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c6bec6695ef2c4637db6f1f2a80507c40bac573.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.1k\\times 0.1k=0.01k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"161\" height=\"15\" /> or 1% each. Thus the blue area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a192085eaaf392df6737fa9516afe7c9d4e910b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{2\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" /> of the total.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2.28alcumus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2(alcumus)\">Solution 2(alcumus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2(alcumus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the side length of the flag be 10, and let each red segment on the border of the flag be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Then the four white triangles can be placed together to form a white square of area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/2/f320c90ddf7cede46c205a5e06a9e3a41933bbf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 - 36 = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> and side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/b/3db16e6b711f76d115876bda920944e3c865a4b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 - 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/c/23c931ecc59877a53fb8694bbfbb226a2a6945c0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(4 cm);  pair[] A, B, C; real t = 0.2;  A[1] = (0,0); A[2] = (1,0); A[3] = (1,1); A[4] = (0,1); B[1] = (t,0); B[2] = (1 - t,0); B[3] = (1,t); B[4] = (1,1 - t); B[5] = (1 - t,1); B[6] = (t,1); B[7] = (0,1 - t); B[8] = (0,t); C[1] = extension(B[1],B[4],B[7],B[2]); C[2] = extension(B[3],B[6],B[1],B[4]); C[3] = extension(B[5],B[8],B[3],B[6]); C[4] = extension(B[7],B[2],B[5],B[8]);  draw(A[1]--A[2]--A[3]--A[4]--cycle); draw(B[1]--B[4]); draw(B[2]--B[7]); draw(B[3]--B[6]); draw(B[5]--B[8]); draw(B[2]--B[3],dashed); draw(shift((1.4,t))*((0,0)--(1 - 2*t,0)--(1 - 2*t,1 - 2*t)--(0,1 - 2*t)--cycle)); draw(shift((1.4,t))*((0,0)--(1 - 2*t,1 - 2*t))); draw(shift((1.4,t))*((1 - 2*t,0)--(0,1 - 2*t)));  label(&quot;$x$&quot;, (A[2] + B[3])/2, E); label(&quot;$x \\sqrt{2}$&quot;, (B[2] + B[3])/2, NW); label(&quot;$10 - 2x$&quot;, (1,0.5), E); [/asy]\" width=\"382\" height=\"192\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/8/e38c915ae3575557869c6385f40a9082bffe01c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10 - 2x)^2 = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"21\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Then the blue area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/351dbc7c434b51202bb380a756a8d4cf44fb9267.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x \\sqrt{2})^2 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"24\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a192085eaaf392df6737fa9516afe7c9d4e910b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{2\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" /> of the area.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME\" title=\"1989 AHSME\">1989 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1989 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?ti